// OWN-6, SEM-7: an operator reads its operands. A place of a moving type is moved only
// where `take` is written, so `a == b` on view parameters is accepted, and `s == s`
// leaves `s` live for the move after it.
// expect: gap cleanup of own values is not built
// expect: gap comparison of this type is not built
fn same(a: String, b: String) -> bool { a == b }
fn eat(take s: String) {}
fn both(take s: String) -> bool {
    let t = s == s
    eat(take s)
    t
}
